[% IF html %]<p>[% END -%]
For a while I have been wondering why the server has been
refusing connections even though my firewall didn't block
the IP I was connecting from... well turns out nginx wasn't
running this whole time :x
[%- IF html %]</p>[% ELSE %]
[% END -%]

[% IF html %]<p>[% END -%]
Sorry for the confusion if anyone thought the server was
down!  Also let me know my firewall rules are too strict
for you... I understand that IP bans can be quite unfair
to people who actually want to access my website but can't
because a few bad actors taint the IP reputation.  If you
are patient know that the IP bans aren't permanent (as
long my ban wears them out -- which is the real point of
banning!  I promise it's not because I hate people, but
bots[% dots %] are annoying. [% FILTER html %]>:c[% END %])
[%- IF html %]</p>[% ELSE %]
[% END -%]
